package\nwith a segment named ",[283,384,314],{}," other than an Enterprise Extension Point, and the capability of every\nEnterprise Extension Point. They live in the module each one belongs to, such as\n",[283,387,388],{},"org.kinotic.domain.internal.api.ee"," in ",[283,391,392],{},"kinotic-domain",".",[288,395,396,406],{},[291,397,398],{},[294,399,400,403],{},[297,401,402],{},"Enterprise Feature",[297,404,405],{},"Free alternative",[304,407,408,424],{},[294,409,410,417],{},[309,411,412,413,416],{},"Azure Key Vault secret storage (",[283,414,415],{},"kinotic.domain.secretStorage.backend: AZURE",")",[309,418,419,420,423],{},"In-memory secret storage (",[283,421,422],{},"backend: IN_MEMORY",", the default), which keeps secrets in process memory and loses them on restart",[294,425,426,429],{},[309,427,428],{},"Okta and Microsoft Entra ID sign-in through an organization's own client, at the organization's login, an application's login or a tenant's login",[309,430,431],{},"Google sign-in through the organization's own client. Microsoft sign-in through Kinotic's managed registration is not an Enterprise Feature",[273,433,434],{},"The org, system and app servers include the Enterprise Features, so the published server images\ncontain them. An Enterprise Feature that is present but not turned on is not in production use, and\nhaving one in an image does not license its production use.",[269,436,438],{"id":437},"license-key","License key",[273,440,441,442,445,446,449,450,453],{},"A server turns an Enterprise Feature on only when its ",[283,443,444],{},"kinotic.ee.licenseKey"," property (the\n",[283,447,448],{},"KINOTIC_EE_LICENSEKEY"," environment variable) holds a License Key from Minds Ignited that lists the\nfeature, or ",[283,451,452],{},"*"," for every feature, and has not expired. The server checks the key when it starts, offline, and logs the licensee,\nexpiry and features it turned on, or why the key is not valid.",[273,455,456,457,460],{},"The local Docker Compose stack in ",[283,458,459],{},"deployment\u002Fdocker-compose\u002F"," sets the Kinotic evaluation license key, which\nturns on every Enterprise Feature until the end of 2036 for development and testing only. The published server images\ncarry no key.",[288,462,463,473],{},[291,464,465],{},[294,466,467,470],{},[297,468,469],{},"Feature named in the key",[297,471,472],{},"Without it",[304,474,475,488],{},[294,476,477,482],{},[309,478,479],{},[283,480,481],{},"AZURE_KEY_VAULT",[309,483,484,485,487],{},"A server set to ",[283,486,415],{}," refuses to start",[294,489,490,495],{},[309,491,492],{},[283,493,494],{},"ENTERPRISE_IDENTITY_PROVIDERS",[309,496,497],{},"Saving or editing an Okta or Microsoft Entra ID configuration that uses an organization's own client is refused. Configurations already saved keep signing people in",[269,499,501],{"id":500},"enterprise-extension-points","Enterprise Extension Points",[273,503,504,505,507,508,511,512,514],{},"Any interface, abstract class, or annotation in a Java package with a segment named ",[283,506,314],{},", such as\n",[283,509,510],{},"org.kinotic.domain.api.ee.services",", or in a directory named ",[283,513,314],{},", is an Enterprise Extension\nPoint. The extension point itself is Elastic-licensed, so you can read it\nand build against it, but the capability it provides is an Enterprise Feature.",[273,516,517],{},"For production use, the license does not permit you to:",[519,520,521,525,531],"ul",{},[522,523,524],"li",{},"implement or extend an Enterprise Extension Point, or use such an implementation, other than\nan Enterprise Implementation or one included in the Elastic-licensed code and used unmodified",[522,526,527,528,530],{},"modify Kinotic to move a type out of an ",[283,529,314],{}," package, or to replace, bypass or wrap an\nEnterprise Extension Point or the code that uses it, so that other software provides its\ncapability",[522,532,533],{},"provide the capability of an Enterprise Extension Point in any other way designed to avoid the\nneed for an enterprise license",[269,535,537],{"id":536},"what-each-use-requires","What each use requires",[288,539,540,550],{},[291,541,542],{},[294,543,544,547],{},[297,545,546],{},"Use",[297,548,549],{},"Requires",[304,551,552,560,568,576],{},[294,553,554,557],{},[309,555,556],{},"Reading, building, modifying and testing the Enterprise Features, locally or in a non-production environment that serves no end users, customers or business operations",[309,558,559],{},"Accepting the Kinotic Enterprise License, which you do by using them",[294,561,562,565],{},[309,563,564],{},"Writing your own implementation of an Enterprise Extension Point for development and testing",[309,566,567],{},"Nothing beyond the Elastic License 2.0 and the Kinotic Additional Limitations",[294,569,570,573],{},[309,571,572],{},"Running an Enterprise Feature in production",[309,574,575],{},"A written agreement with Minds Ignited that permits that use, and a valid License Key wherever Minds Ignited has issued one for that feature",[294,577,578,581],{},[309,579,580],{},"Running Kinotic in production without the Enterprise Features",[309,582,583],{},"The Elastic License 2.0 and the Kinotic Additional Limitations: no agreement, provided each Enterprise Extension Point runs only the implementation included in the Elastic-licensed code, unmodified",[273,585,586],{},"A written agreement that permits only limited purposes, such as evaluation or a proof of concept,\nlicenses production use for those purposes alone. The Enterprise Features may be redistributed\nonly unmodified, with the Kinotic Enterprise License, as part of a copy of Kinotic distributed\nunder the Elastic License 2.0, and may not be offered to third parties as a hosted or managed\nservice, and the Elastic License\n2.0 forbids offering Kinotic itself as a hosted or managed service that gives users access to a\nsubstantial set of its features.",[273,588,589,590,393],{},"To arrange an enterprise agreement, contact Minds Ignited through ",[277,591,594],{"href":592,"rel":593},"https:\u002F\u002Fkinotic.ai",[281],"kinotic.ai",[269,596,598],{"id":597},"contributions","Contributions",[273,600,601,602,607,608,393],{},"Contributors accept the\n",[277,603,606],{"href":604,"rel":605},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fkinotic-ai\u002Fkinotic\u002Fblob\u002Fdevelop\u002FCLA.md",[281],"Kinotic Contributor License Agreement",",\nwhich lets Minds Ignited license a contribution under either license. See\n",[277,609,212],{"href":610},"\u002Fplatform\u002Fcontributing#licensing",{"title":612,"searchDepth":613,"depth":613,"links":614},"",2,[615,616,617,618,619,620],{"id":271,"depth":613,"text":26},{"id":378,"depth":613,"text":379},{"id":437,"depth":613,"text":438},{"id":500,"depth":613,"text":501},{"id":536,"depth":613,"text":537},{"id":597,"depth":613,"text":598},"Which parts of Kinotic are Enterprise Features, what running them in production requires, and how the license treats substitute implementations.","md",null,{},{"icon":262},{"title":259,"description":621},"j_Vx2dXB0f_DoEnHMomHX_kQtFT_SEGlLgKDvHnl5Cw",[629,623],{"title":254,"path":255,"stem":256,"description":630,"icon":257,"children":-1},"How Kinotic inventories, scans and gates the container images it publishes, and where the evidence for each control is kept.",1794205773606]